    <section>
      <h2>15. Interview Preparation — চাকরির ইন্টারভিউ</h2>

      <h3>Q1. What is Data?</h3>
      <p>
        <strong>Answer:</strong> Data refers to raw facts, observations,
        measurements, or records collected about an entity, event, or
        activity.
      </p>
      <p>
        উদাহরণ: Customer Name, Product Price, Order Date এবং Transaction Amount।
      </p>

      <h3>Q2. What is Data Analytics?</h3>
      <p>
        <strong>Answer:</strong> Data Analytics is the process of
        examining and interpreting data to identify patterns, answer
        questions, generate insights, and support decision-making.
      </p>

      <h3>Q3. Why is Data Analytics important for businesses?</h3>
      <p>
        <strong>Answer:</strong> Data Analytics helps businesses
        understand performance, identify problems, improve operations,
        understand customers, manage risks, and make evidence-based decisions.
      </p>

      <h3>Q4. What is a Dataset?</h3>
      <p>
        <strong>Answer:</strong> A Dataset is an organized collection
        of related data records. It may contain rows and columns,
        files, or other structured collections of information.
      </p>

      <h3>Q5. What is a Business Insight?</h3>
      <p>
        <strong>Answer:</strong> A Business Insight is a meaningful
        finding derived from data analysis that helps an organization
        understand an issue or identify an opportunity.
      </p>

      <h3>Q6. What is the difference between Revenue and Profit?</h3>
      <p>
        <strong>Answer:</strong> Revenue is the income generated from
        business activities, while Profit is the amount remaining
        after deducting relevant costs.
      </p>

      <h3>Q7. Does more data always mean better decisions?</h3>
      <p>
        <strong>Answer:</strong> No. Data quality, relevance,
        completeness, accuracy, and correct interpretation are more
        important than data volume alone.
      </p>

      <h3>Q8. How would you start analyzing declining sales?</h3>
      <p>
        <strong>Answer:</strong> I would first clarify the business
        problem, define the analysis period, collect relevant sales
        and business data, validate the data, identify useful metrics,
        investigate possible causes, and communicate evidence-based
        recommendations.
      </p>

